{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0bf96c9f545e21013613668df7059b1be652419401bc2439d188c07d4db841d2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f28931a9fc4723e01900a833ac8b93c5b224952af74ffc8b0da4fa08864594ef"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"Verification notes are agent-reported and validated for structure, identity, scope, idempotency, and progress rules, but the server does not independently prove source code or deployments passed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e614fceb948b9c17a8db38686ffd89d1975719960b9002ebb55fff992091592","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8de6082d01a319d91da849e14544d54c6dd8cd6c7313951a66aa59c8bd67aea2","slc_f28931a9fc4723e01900a833ac8b93c5b224952af74ffc8b0da4fa08864594ef"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"The released MCP surface contains exactly two tools: project_os_get_context for scoped context reads and project_os_append_progress for validated, idempotent progress appends.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_10ff73852c2d3d163a52758640ad407003784c72df654bb915656190d8a43136","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_12ce8d16bb894d46ebbad983348c688e7010cb2b52a5a3a842b9019c30b753da","slc_3ba6af0ccd0ee157c356adb6358ab93b829562885e2aa46519457b5b29fd5ad9"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"The open-source design keeps private infrastructure behind replaceable adapter boundaries for Git, AI provider, knowledge base, and deployment/reverse proxy, with local JSON persistence for simple evaluation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d9f3f90adfad3d749fcc33d51447b9f783542095e435499bc12986616b5c9db","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7e7ec521645c60a02cc52ce72206f09f07f030b7fbdfa937b1736e05cf3a8507","slc_e3a2e9f948d0503814fbeec20136921160fa747d5d311818eb6d4c5dd68de0e3"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"An Agent API endpoint accepts progress events via POST with X-Project-Key and Idempotency-Key headers, including verification notes, progress percentage, and next step.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_505d5baa55fb3ede538bd2052b62e1e06fd6fb18d838d148cb4a6cf6ae650743","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20b76dca21af01f7c23693428afda79613c3eb2da1a78da6eb781301e0cd5955","slc_4f0213d039b4a5ac108d7854afbb9bcb3b95a7ee865b8ffbab46113e6c724ee3"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"Version 0.3.0 adds a fail-closed first-run contract: the MCP process verifies credential, project binding, scopes, and the exact two-tool surface before Codex uses it, with a project-level config allowlisting only released tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_82308b18879b1cb426a3bb84259dfdebd0e9dc5a54e8009b41466598cf90cd2e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_682e6a87721eb1ce2ac423618b3adf524082d4f4c2d4e87424862f667ef79a12"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"The stack is React, Vite, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS on the frontend with Node.js and Express on the backend, persisting to local JSON files by default under an Apache-2.0 license.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_875b5289194917f8ebaa709322274ff9972ab45318e387a1a2d1f5436d3cdc14","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25a410c60043ab3b5e28f373fe7b4b1feccae11d9183423cc8aeabb6e23f338b","slc_836b171474a0c84317e95c21e2893eb0a54f7d8692a0911a908b4e14e3295d9d","slc_b0b1268543e2a2a41d40d1e9cc381b5d8ad2a31dc3c39b52e48298e2ddcecfc8"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"The server creates a local Git-backed project record for kickoff, progress, issues, and handoff files, with important progress linked to Git commits as the durable record.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9af94a8357694dc42a69c58861d1d1e0fd2701f6da0d837477594db662c1fa36","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c826e0e148c9d2159276c309aa2ebc953c6085895997d7e0d3ab5b4ca0ea391c"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"AI credentials are short-lived (24 hours or 7 days), revocable independently, stored only as hashes, and cannot access members, keys, deletion, publication, or deployment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bdb1c7199cce60d79e28e986dc1158d3715f255a802840c364e77a0a05701a67","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f28931a9fc4723e01900a833ac8b93c5b224952af74ffc8b0da4fa08864594ef"],"source_ids":["src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"The product does not run Codex, monitor sessions automatically, control a Codex account, or modify an existing source repository; its Git commits belong to the local Project OS record repository.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5ee7eba328c2168569c7a435e4c6b2e8c81109864dc019699b222a873cbe029","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_281e21fffcec7841c5459e6e12f12dfbc01fb1a592db86d254bccff8efae9605","slc_5327a902605cc321afbfed6724efab1c84d9b79dd743d2f728ab0c56eead24fe"],"source_ids":["src_51b598ac71105681abcb22f8eb78d374","src_59e7420d879c56ec92e7ff5630094eef"],"text":"High-risk actions such as payment, deletion, role changes, publication, deployment, and rollback stay outside the MCP surface and require explicit human confirmation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_db3b24e29683f5708b493e5bd57d102e200e4fcd1e758d41836aec85ccd24a52","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_27c97920f5d717dba57ef960aeb3c3e19f2b55ef6e5a4866a37c2ae3f057d698","slc_4a9cec337887387dda71caf6959c4d6d8e499d1c6eaa6e7ac7d3785d0b1a46de"],"source_ids":["src_51b598ac71105681abcb22f8eb78d374"],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md instructs contributors to work one vertical slice at a time, use pnpm, run pnpm run check before committing, and inspect affected UI in light and dark themes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","created_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f00787d89e66c27b7e7dea63559e294e777c2d02b11d20e25efa9eb4ace123e9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"herry2059/project-os-for-codex@3cb909ab9f61 snapshot 6d015e25229802c1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ffce5ac73f8cc15c51b8abaa2522dc0013ca18e5a76ebafd75f1044adaedff90"],"source_ids":["src_51b598ac71105681abcb22f8eb78d374"],"text":"Repository development practice: the Codex session protocol requires calling project_os_get_context before planning, running pnpm codex:doctor on failure, and only appending progress after verifying one vertical slice.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:03:21Z","updated_by_operation":"op_c2f7300587ae444b8ff3b0c1c38b5b5f"}
